mod:pointer_returned_target;
// A POINTER A FUNCTION RETURNED IS A WRITE TO SOMEONE (DEF-591; landing 177d2b4, row 6): each module one face, refused at the write
// through the returned pointer. A getter's `pass @w.l` reaches the caller as all of `w`, so a write through what it returned is a write
// of that whole target, in the frame and in a callee's summary (`xu12l`, `xu12r`, `xu10`, `xu10l`, `xu11l`, `pr1c`, `zc2k`, `zc2r`,
// `zc3k`, `zc3r`). A pointer read out of a holder is a target by its pointee (`x72d1`). A pass-through getter's result handed to a writer
// writes its argument (`zn11i`). On a7f1c1b each is 236 at -O0 and -O2, and 97 under the freed-heap detector.
